# redox-os/base @ 8f576d27: initfs debug console for the Pinebook Pro port
#
# Target repository : https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/base.git
# Base commit       : 8f576d27ee5d028157b001e320affc7b1ec2736b (main, 2026-11)
# Reason            : interim serial console (experiment 5). The Pinebook Pro
#                     boot stops at the initfs phase because there is no
#                     microSD (DW MMC) driver yet, so no root filesystem and
#                     no shell. This patch adds `debugsh`, a small static
#                     initfs daemon that opens the kernel `debug` scheme
#                     (/scheme/debug), gives the UART line discipline (echo,
#                     backspace) and a few built-ins (ls/cat/echo>/hexdump/
#                     env/exec), so schemes and initfs binaries can be poked
#                     from the serial console before storage works.
#
# Contents:
#   * debugsh/                  new initfs-only crate (static binary)
#   * Makefile                  add debugsh to INITFS_BINS
#   * Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock    workspace member + lock entry
#   * init.initfs.d/95_debugsh.service        service (aarch64 only)
#   * init.initfs.d/90_initfs.target          start it with the initfs target
#   * init.initfs.d/40_pcid-spawner-initfs.service, init.d/00_pcid-spawner.service:
#     gate pcid-spawner to x86/x86_64: pcid's PCI 3.0 configuration-space
#     fallback is `todo!()` on aarch64 and panics (experiment 4). Rootfs-phase
#     service gated now so boot does not regress once storage works.
#
# Apply from recipes/core/base/source:  git apply <this file>
